### Try these with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or copy the curl equivalents).
### Mock auth: pick who you are with the x-mock-user header. No header = alex@example.com.

@base = http://localhost:5000/api

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Who am I
GET {{base}}/me
x-mock-user: maria@example.com

### Sessions near Grace Hall (inside the 100 m radius) -> returns "Sunday service"
POST {{base}}/sessions/nearby
x-mock-user: maria@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 14.58361, "lng": 120.97916, "accuracy": 12 }

### Far away -> empty list
POST {{base}}/sessions/nearby
x-mock-user: maria@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 14.7, "lng": 121.2, "accuracy": 12 }

### Weak GPS -> 422 GPS_TOO_WEAK
POST {{base}}/sessions/nearby
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 14.58361, "lng": 120.97916, "accuracy": 250 }

### Check in (replace SESSION_ID with an id printed by `npm run seed`)
POST {{base}}/sessions/SESSION_ID/check-in
x-mock-user: maria@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 14.58361, "lng": 120.97916, "accuracy": 12 }

### Passcode session check-in
POST {{base}}/sessions/PASSCODE_SESSION_ID/check-in
x-mock-user: maria@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 14.6538, "lng": 121.0685, "accuracy": 10, "passcode": "1234" }

### My check-in history
GET {{base}}/me/history
x-mock-user: maria@example.com

### Creator: my sessions
GET {{base}}/sessions/mine

### Creator: create a session (email-restricted)
POST {{base}}/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Math review",
  "category": "School",
  "venue": "Room 12",
  "startsAt": "2026-10-26T09:00:00.000Z",
  "endsAt": "2026-10-26T11:00:00.000Z",
  "lat": 14.5995,
  "lng": 120.9842,
  "radius": 60,
  "verification": "email",
  "allowedEmails": ["maria@example.com", "ben@example.com"]
}

### Creator: records, manual add, CSV
GET {{base}}/sessions/SESSION_ID/records

###
POST {{base}}/sessions/SESSION_ID/records
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Walk-in Guest" }

###
GET {{base}}/sessions/SESSION_ID/export.csv

### Creator: live attendance (Server-Sent Events). EventSource cannot send headers, so use ?as=
GET {{base}}/sessions/SESSION_ID/live?as=alex@example.com
